cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "NEXUS: a compiler, CPU simulators, parallel and GPU models and a Verilog MIPS core covering six computer-systems courses"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - given-names: "George David"
    family-names: "Tsitlauri"
    affiliation: "Department of Informatics and Telecommunications, University of Thessaly"
date-released: 2026-10-05
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/gdtsitlauri/nexus-platform"
abstract: >-
  A C++20 and Verilog project covering six computer-systems courses with executable, tested code: a
  NexusLang-to-MIPS compiler with linear-scan register allocation, SSA/SCCP and polyhedral loop
  transformations; automata, LL/LR/Earley parsing and Hindley-Milner type inference; MIPS execution
  models from a functional interpreter to a Tomasulo core with reorder buffer and SMT; multicore,
  network-on-chip and SIMT GPU models; bit-exact IEEE-754 soft float; and a synthesisable 5-stage
  pipelined MIPS core co-simulated against the simulators.
keywords: [compilers, computer architecture, MIPS, simulation, Tomasulo, polyhedral, Verilog, education]
